        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-08T14:57:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The goal here was that the SkQP flag would control the naming of the tests, and that our regular expressions in `unit_tests.txt` could leverage that naming. \n\nWhen the SkQP flag is set, the test names are plain: `SkSLTestFeature_GPU` (or CPU)\n\nWhen the SkQP flag is absent, the test names will always have a NoSkQP suffix: `SkSLTestFeature_GPU_NoSkQP`\n\nThis allows SkQP to filter on `SkSL.+_NoSkQP` to eliminate all the non-SkQP tests without maintaining an exhaustive list.\n\nEvery time a test is added to SkSLTest.cpp, the flag choices are front and center (very first param to `SKSL_TEST`) so it ensures that we don\u0027t add tests without at least considering its presence or absence in SkQP.",
      "parentUuid": "7cdeafbe_f9a69dd6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 298,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 298,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "670e8c33326e51adeb027b5b5fa58e64783451da",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
