      "writtenOn": "2022-03-08T16:14:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK, I wasn\u0027t aware that we wanted to delete `unit_tests.txt` entirely. In that case, granted, this doesn\u0027t quite get us there. (I think you could make a compelling case for hard-coding a global skqp rule that skips over any test with a `_NoSkQP` suffix on its name, but that\u0027s neither here nor there.)\n\nAdding member variables to Test is easy; I can take care of that. There are two relevant bits that I can think of: \"this is an SkSL test\" and \"SkQP should run this test\". They seem pretty independent. Should I add both bits?\n\nRight now we have two bools, should I make it into an int of flag-bits instead? Or maybe an Options struct? Otherwise we\u0027re going to have a gaggle of bools, which becomes error-prone and hard to read.",
